< **Rule:** native structs retain declaration order, each field rounded up to its alignment, aggregate alignment the maximum (1 for empty), and final size rounded up. Empty aggregates have size 0/alignment 1. Arrays have size `n × size(T)` and alignment `align(T)`, including `n = 0`. Fixed-width integer storage respects value width; alignment is target-defined. Q4.5 decides only StaticStr’s explicit pointer/byte-length FFI adapter, without an internal ABI promise. Q3.1–Q3.4 and Q4.6–Q4.7 decide view roots, loans and ranges, not their physical representation. Text length counts UTF-8 bytes. TYPE-3 Text owns immutable bytes, never aliases another value’s buffer, and is linear. Its ownership, allocator dependency and sufficient release context must survive representation; Q4.5’s FFI adapter does not fix Text’s internal size. No universal two-word Text layout is frozen. A common shared/mutable view representation is a proposal, not a decided rule. Defer its concrete layout to the view/layout slice, preserving the decided second-class semantics; no two-word view ABI is frozen. Address-space selection is explicit profile metadata, including program-memory text: no silent cast to data pointers. `Secret<T>` has T's layout, without implying constant time.
